{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_011CdyCcN2gzFdWjfLrHNsrw","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"# Fix Plan\n\n## 1. **Declare the numeric contract in the mapper**\n   - **File:** `golden/mapper.ts`\n   - **Change:** Round the `irr` field to 1e-9 (9 decimal places) before serialization, matching the product spec's stated behavioral tolerance for all monetary projections.\n   - **Concrete code pattern:**\n     ```typescript\n     irr: Math.round(irr * 1e9) / 1e9\n     ```\n\n## 2. **Regenerate the baseline on Node 20**\n   - **Command:** `npm test -- --update-golden` (or equivalent) on Node 20\n   - **Rationale:** Freeze the normalized contract into `golden/projections.json`, eliminating the last-bit FP noise that varies across runtimes\n\n## 3. **Verify the gate passes on both environments**\n   - **Command:** Run the full CI suite (both Node 20 and Node 22 jobs)\n   - **Expected outcome:** Both jobs green; the 41 deltas (1e-14 to 2e-13) all round to the same normalized value across both runtimes\n\n## 4. **Document the decision**\n   - **File:** `docs/testing.md` or a commit message\n   - **Content:** Record that `irr` normalization to 1e-9 in the mapper is the durable remedy for environment-noise portability, and explain it fulfills the claimed tolerance in the product spec\n\n---\n\n**Why this fixes it:** The doctrine distinguishes frozen noise (a trap) from a declared contract (the remedy). The baseline inherited Node 20's FP noise; the mapper had no contract. Normalizing in the mapper before freezing makes the contract explicit and coarse enough to absorb environment divergence (1e-14–2e-13 noise ≪ 1e-9 tolerance), while staying fine enough to catch real bugs."}],"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":689,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0,"cache_read_input_tokens":0,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":448,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"}}
